# Requêtes de test des routes d'authentification (extension VSCode REST Client).

@server = http://localhost:3000

### Inscription -> 201 { token }
# @name register
POST {{server}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "charlie@vinci.be",
  "password": "charlie",
  "firstName": "Charlie",
  "lastName": "Leroy"
}

### Inscription avec un email déjà utilisé -> 409
POST {{server}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@vinci.be",
  "password": "x",
  "firstName": "Alice",
  "lastName": "Bis"
}

### Inscription avec un corps invalide -> 400
POST {{server}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "pas-un-email",
  "password": ""
}

### Connexion -> 200 { token }
# @name login
POST {{server}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@vinci.be",
  "password": "alice"
}

### Connexion administrateur -> 200 { token }
# @name adminLogin
POST {{server}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@vinci.be",
  "password": "admin"
}

### Mauvais mot de passe -> 401
POST {{server}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@vinci.be",
  "password": "pas-le-bon"
}

### Utilisateur connecté -> 200 { id, email, firstName, lastName, role }
GET {{server}}/auth/me
Authorization: {{login.response.body.token}}

### Sans token -> 401
GET {{server}}/auth/me
